;
; How Orrery files a sky observation, in MYRA: its number, the body seen
; (1..8 a planet, 101..108 a star of the model's table), when (seconds
; since 1970; twelve digits reach the last second of year 9999), and where
; in the sky, altitude and azimuth in millidegrees. The model says what the
; values may mean (orrery_rules.h OR4); this says whether they make a record.
^ZXOBS(obs:i9) = body:i4! ^ time:i12! ^ alt:i6! ^ az:i6!
